From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 01:38:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/28] udf: make database context reuse cancellation-safe

Preserve upstream module-wide experimental_reuseContext behavior for queries
and mutations while keeping actions and HTTP actions fresh at the database-UDF
boundary. Recheck the typed decision at validation, scheduler-affinity,
context-take, and context-save boundaries.

Carry an explicit caller-drop signal through queued and same-isolate recursive
UDF execution. Give separately scheduled nested UDF callbacks their own signal
and publish cancellation before their response receiver closes when the parent
stops waiting. Recheck cancellation and termination after the final microtask
checkpoint immediately before publishing a reusable context, while keeping the
documented post-check timeout race explicit.

Cover conversion and cancellation primitives and document the generic
adoption, source-purity, and rollback contract without an application module
allowlist.
